.TH SHUTTLE 1 "2026-11-03" "Shuttle" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shuttle \- record and export signed append-only workflow runs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shuttle
.RI [ --require-existing-keys ] " command " [ arguments ]
.br
.B shuttle
.BR --help " | " --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shuttle records workflow definitions, runs and signed transitions in a local
append-only log. Run state is folded from that log. Export sends records to a
separately configured Quipu service; local state buffers records until export.
Installing this package does not start a service, generate keys or configure
credentials. Network operations require an explicitly configured service.
.SH COMMANDS
Use
.B shuttle command --help
for the options of each command.
.TP
.B prime
Print agent orientation and local read-only state.
.TP
.B version
Print the installed version.
.TP
.BI "keys init " agent " [--workflow workflow]"
Create or show an agent key and print registration Turtle. Public-key
registration is a separate operation; Shuttle does not register its own keys.
.TP
.BI "define " file " [--at timestamp]"
Record a workflow definition from a JSON file.
.TP
.BI "start " definition " run --agent agent [--at timestamp]"
Start a run of a recorded workflow definition.
.TP
.BI "advance " run " --step step --agent agent [--at timestamp]"
Perform one signed workflow transition.
.TP
.BI "status " [run]
Show state folded from the local log for one run or all runs.
.TP
.BI "reconcile " "[run] --agent agent"
Create seeds for seed steps and advance runs whose seed has closed.
.TP
.B export [--strict]
Drain the local log into Quipu windows. Strict mode stops at the first record
that cannot be posted, leaving it and all later records unexported.
.TP
.BI "verify " run " [--identity-graph IRI]"
Re-verify a run's signatures from the graph.
.TP
.BI "import-run " file " --agent agent"
Import foreign transition JSONL as a signed run.
.TP
.BI "freeze-window " month " [--agent agent]"
Freeze a completed window through Quipu.
.TP
.BI "scheduled " action " --config file"
Run the strict scheduled-run process port. Actions are
.BR admit , " started" , " finished" " and " publish .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --require-existing-keys
Refuse missing or unsafe local keys throughout the command; never generate keys.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Show the installed version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHUTTLE_STATE_DIR
Override the default local state directory,
.IR ~/.local/state/shuttle .
.TP
.B SHUTTLE_KEY_DIR
Override the default signing key directory,
.IR ~/.config/shuttle/keys .
.TP
.B QUIPU_SERVER
Quipu service URL. The default is
.IR http://localhost:3030 .
.TP
.B QUIPU_AUTH_TOKEN
Bearer token for Quipu. Treat this value as a secret.
.TP
.B QUIPU_AUTH_TOKEN_FILE
Path to a token file, used when QUIPU_AUTH_TOKEN is absent.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/shuttle/runs.jsonl
Append-only workflow log. Preserve records that have not yet been exported.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/shuttle/export-watermark.json
Tracks the portion of the log already exported.
.TP
.I ~/.config/shuttle/keys
Agent signing keys. Preserve these keys; replacing one changes signing identity.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Invalid arguments and refused operations return a
nonzero status with a diagnostic on standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1)
